<div class="deep-dive-body">
<p class="lede"><span class="drop">T</span>he main lesson taught the old danger: a p-value plus human flexibility can turn noise into literature. This appendix looks forward. The sharpest post-2020 work is not merely “use AI carefully” or “report confidence intervals.” It is a deeper shift: <strong>validity is being moved outside the model, outside the analyst’s discretion, and sometimes outside the raw data itself.</strong> The new tools wrap black boxes in guarantees, split exploration from inference, keep tests valid while people peek, correct AI labels with human truth, quantify privacy noise, and audit the research machine itself. They are powerful. They are also easy to oversell.</p>
